      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0176",
      "sequence": 188,
      "meaning": "In due time, Śiva says, that king and his whole company became night-rangers. Pratāpabhānu was born as the formidable Rāvaṇa, with ten heads and twenty mighty arms; his younger brother Arimardana became the immensely strong Kumbhakarṇa. The minister Dharmaruci became their younger half-brother Vibhīṣaṇa, renowned throughout the world as a wise devotee of Viṣṇu. The king’s sons and servants became numerous dreadful demons, shape-shifting villains of many kinds—crooked, terrifying, undiscerning, merciless, violent, sinful and tormentors of the world. Though born into Pulastya’s pure, matchless lineage, the Brahmins’ curse made them embodiments of sin.",
