    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0177",
      "sequence": 189,
      "meaning": "The three brothers perform austerities so fearsome they cannot be described. Pleased, Brahmā approaches and asks them to choose boons. Ten-headed Rāvaṇa grasps his feet and asks immunity from death at anyone’s hands, dismissing monkeys and humans as beneath concern; Brahmā grants it in recognition of his great penance. Seeing Kumbhakarṇa, Brahmā wonders that daily feeding such a villain would depopulate the world, so he prompts Sarasvatī to turn the demon’s thought; Kumbhakarṇa asks instead for sleep lasting six months. Vibhīṣaṇa asks for pure love of the Lord’s lotus feet.",
