    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0178",
      "sequence": 190,
      "meaning": "After giving the boons, Brahmā departs and the delighted brothers return home. Maya gives Rāvaṇa his supremely beautiful daughter Mandodarī in marriage, knowing he will rule the demons, and Rāvaṇa also arranges marriages for his two brothers. On Mount Trikūṭa amid the ocean stands a vast, inaccessible fortress built by Brahmā and adorned anew by the demon Maya with limitless golden, jewelled mansions. More delightful than serpent-inhabited Bhogavatī or Indra’s Amarāvatī, the splendid city is famed as Laṅkā. A deep ocean encircles all four sides and strong golden, jewel-inlaid walls defy description. In each cosmic cycle, by Hari’s prompting, a mighty, brilliant demon lord resides there with his forces.",
