    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0179",
      "sequence": 191,
      "meaning": "Powerful demons once living in Laṅkā had been destroyed by the gods; now Indra’s command has placed tens of millions of Kubera’s Yakṣas there as guards. Hearing this, ten-headed Rāvaṇa marches with his army and surrounds the fortress. Seeing his formidable host, the Yakṣas flee for their lives. Rāvaṇa inspects the naturally beautiful and inaccessible city, finds it exceptionally pleasing, and makes it his capital. He assigns fitting homes to each follower and makes all night-rangers prosperous. He later attacks Kubera and captures the Puṣpaka aerial car; as a sport he even lifts Mount Kailāsa, as though weighing it against his arm-strength, and departs delighted.",
