    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0180",
      "sequence": 192,
      "meaning": "Rāvaṇa’s happiness, wealth, sons, allies, victories, renown, strength, intelligence and greatness increase ceaselessly, like greed swelling with every gain. His immensely strong brother Kumbhakarṇa has no known rival; he drinks and sleeps for six months, and when awake terrifies all three worlds—were he to eat daily, he would quickly devastate the universe. His elder son Meghanāda is foremost among warriors, so invincible that no one faces him in battle and heaven is repeatedly defeated. Kumukha, Akampana, Kuliśarada, Dhūmaketu, Atikāya and the other hosts of champions could each conquer the world alone.",
